>
  <h1>Get started</h1>
  <p>
    Strata is a database you embed in your program. There is no server to run and nothing to
    configure first: you install a binary, point it at a directory, and that directory is a
    database.
  </p>
  <p>
    Start with <a href="/docs/get-started/installation">Installation</a>. If you would rather try it
    without installing anything, the <a href="/playground">playground</a> runs the real engine compiled
    to wasm, in your browser.
  </p>
  <p>
    Once it is running, <a href="/docs/learn/introduction">Introduction to StrataDB</a> is the shortest
    explanation of what you have, and <a href="/docs/get-started/agents">Agents</a> covers wiring it into
    a coding agent over MCP.
  </p>
  <SectionLanding section="Get Started" />
</DocsLayout>
